-- SUM-TYPE-FIELDS-SPEC §1.1: what a partial field read says when it DOES reach
-- run time.
--
-- This file is here under `ok/` for an uncomfortable reason: it checks clean
-- and then dies. That is hole (a) of §5.1 item 1, and the only residual hole in
-- the clause-column narrowing itself — an UNTYPED `GIVEN` column is still an
-- inference variable when the narrowing table is built, which has to happen
-- before the body is checked, so the column keeps the old suppression and S2
-- cannot refuse the read. Write `GIVEN s IS AN Actor` instead and the same
-- program is refused at check time; that is
-- `not-ok/tc/partial-projection-fallthrough.l4`.
--
-- §5.1 item 1 lists a SECOND permissive hole, which is not this mechanism and
-- is not witnessed here: a hand-written NULLARY declaration spelled with the
-- desugarer's reserved `__pm_fallthrough_` name. It has no corpus fixture
-- because pinning it would mean shipping that spelling in the corpus.
--
-- The hole is why the RUN-TIME message still matters, and this file is what
-- pins it. What it used to say was:
--
--     The value Agent reached a CONSIDER that has no branch for it.
--     Add a WHEN branch for this case, or a catch-all OTHERWISE branch.
--     The typechecker's exhaustiveness warning lists all missing branches.
--
-- Every sentence of which sent the reader somewhere that does not exist. There
-- is no CONSIDER in this file: the one being fallen off is the selector closure
-- the evaluator synthesises for `monthly_rent`, one arm per DECLARING
-- constructor. There is nowhere to add a WHEN branch. And no exhaustiveness
-- warning was emitted — the clause group below is perfectly exhaustive; the
-- partiality is in the selector, which the checker never warned about because
-- it is not in the source. Read the golden for what it says now.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord
    Agent
    Tenant   HAS monthly_rent IS A NUMBER

GIVEN s
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE rent Landlord IS 0
DECIDE rent s        IS s's monthly_rent

-- The clauses cover `Landlord` and then everything, so `Agent` lands in clause
-- 2 and the read is a `monthly_rent` of an `Agent`.
#EVAL rent Agent

-- The same read on a value that DOES declare the field is not affected: the
-- selector is total on its own declaring constructors.
#EVAL rent (Tenant OF 1500)
#EVAL rent Landlord
